From b593a3e6365d02a88375b777c86979ea11e3a7b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Dutton <chris@bigcove.io>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 09:22:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 11/16] firmware: do not register a raw mgmt forwarding mask
 for the SoftAP

esp-hosted NG feeds hostapd's auth/assoc/action frames through the
wpa_ap_rx_mgmt callback its patched libnet80211 calls from the SoftAP SME;
it only uses esp_wifi_register_mgmt_frame_internal() for STA-side
scan/assoc frames. Registering the AP subtypes there as well made the
library hand the frames over raw and skip its own station admission: the
host-added node never became a real associated station
(esp_wifi_ap_get_sta_aid "not found"), and EAPOL message 1 was never
transmitted, so clients looped on auth/assoc (hardware-observed
2026-10-09).
---
 firmware/main/trellis_wifi_ap.c | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/firmware/main/trellis_wifi_ap.c b/firmware/main/trellis_wifi_ap.c
index 241b519..e965cb9 100644
--- a/firmware/main/trellis_wifi_ap.c
+++ b/firmware/main/trellis_wifi_ap.c
@@ -270,9 +270,16 @@ uint8_t trellis_wifi_ap_start(const uint8_t *args, uint16_t arglen)
         return TRELLIS_CTRL_ERR_ERADIO;
     }
 
-    /* Forward auth/assoc/action mgmt frames to the host authenticator; the
-     * wpa_ap_rx_mgmt callback (trellis_wifi_host.c) turns them into events. */
-    esp_wifi_register_mgmt_frame_internal(TRELLIS_AP_MGMT_RX_MASK, 0);
+    /* The host authenticator receives auth/assoc/action/deauth frames through
+     * the wpa_ap_rx_mgmt callback (trellis_wifi_host.c), which esp-hosted
+     * NG's patched libnet80211 invokes from its SoftAP SME. Do NOT also
+     * register a raw forwarding mask (esp_wifi_register_mgmt_frame_internal)
+     * for these subtypes as earlier revisions did: esp-hosted only uses that
+     * mask for STA-side scan/assoc frames, and with it set in AP mode the
+     * library stops running station admission itself, so the associated
+     * client never gets a usable node - esp_wifi_ap_get_sta_aid() fails and
+     * EAPOL message 1 of the 4-way handshake is never transmitted
+     * (hardware-observed 2026-10-09). */
 
     trellis_reassembly_reset(&s_ap_data_reasm);
 
